// The js device (devices/js.ent, QuickJS-ng in devices/quickjs): values
// to and from JSON (UTF-8 kept), errors with where they were, a loop
// stopped by its time (and no `catch` stopping that), memory run out
// (twice, and let go of each time),
// recursion too deep, the context used after each; no std, os or
// import; two contexts apart; random bytes; require (each source run
// once); a promise rejected that nothing handles; calls of the program
// answered and refused, awaited; timers in the order they are due, one
// cleared, an interval; a handle closed is none, and a new one another.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/js/device.ent > %t.out 2>&1
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.out

// CHECK: value: 3
// CHECK-NEXT: object: {"x":[1,"é",null],"y":{"z":true}}
// CHECK-NEXT: undefined: []
// CHECK-NEXT: set: true "Zoë2"
// CHECK-NEXT: get: {"name":"Zoë","n":[1,2.5]}
// CHECK-NEXT: set bad: false
// CHECK-NEXT: syntax: [] SyntaxError: unexpected token in expression: ';'
// CHECK-NEXT:     at bad.js:1:9
// CHECK-NEXT: thrown: TypeError: cannot read property 'x' of null
// CHECK-NEXT:     at f (throw.js:1:15)
// CHECK-NEXT:     at <eval> (throw.js:2:1)
// CHECK-NEXT: thrown text: Uncaught plain
// CHECK-NEXT: ok after: "fine"[]
// CHECK-NEXT: loop: [] interrupted
// CHECK-NEXT: loop catch:  interrupted
// CHECK-NEXT: after loop: 42
// CHECK-NEXT: memory: out of memory
// CHECK-NEXT: after memory: "ok"
// CHECK-NEXT: memory again: out of memory
// CHECK-NEXT: after again: "ok"
// CHECK-NEXT: deep: RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded
// CHECK: no std: "undefined undefined undefined undefined"
// CHECK-NEXT: import: [] not handled: ReferenceError: could not load module 'x'
// CHECK-NEXT: apart: "undefined"
// CHECK-NEXT: random: "16 true"
// CHECK-NEXT: require: "3 5 1"
// CHECK-NEXT: require none: ReferenceError: no module 'nope'
// CHECK: rejected: [] not handled: TypeError: no
// CHECK-NEXT:     at <eval> (r.js:1:20)
// CHECK-NEXT: host gone: "undefined"
// CHECK-NEXT: pending: true
// CHECK-NEXT: call: add {"a":2,"b":3}
// CHECK-NEXT: call: fail 1
// CHECK-NEXT: log: ["queued","add 5","fail refused","micro","t10","t30","ticks 3"]
// CHECK-NEXT: pending at end: 0 true
// CHECK-NEXT: closed: [] 0 []
// CHECK-NEXT: new handle: true "undefined"
